# Derived from the supplied sky_beta_course_vio_range.params; SITL ONLY.
# Local CAD/VIO flight needs one consistent world height through raised
# obstacles. The supplied real-aircraft range-height doctrine is not changed.
# GPS-DENIED, EXTERNAL VISION (VIO) — SITL ONLY. Never push to a real aircraft
# through this tool: hardware carries its own doctrine (BEAM_OWNER, failsafes).
# Format: sysid compid NAME VALUE TYPE  (6 = INT32, 9 = REAL32), QGC style,
# as read by the toolkit's ACK-verified MAVLink loader.
#
# Source: PX4 v1.17 pinned SITL (src/modules/ekf2/params_*.yaml):
#   EKF2_GPS_CTRL  bitmask 0 lon/lat, 1 alt, 2 3D vel, 3 dual-antenna yaw
#   EKF2_EV_CTRL   bitmask 0 horizontal pos, 1 vertical pos, 2 3D vel, 3 yaw
#   EKF2_HGT_REF   0 baro, 1 GPS, 2 range, 3 vision
#   EKF2_MAG_TYPE  0 automatic, 1 heading, 5 none, 6 init-only
#   EKF2_EV_NOISE_MD 0 = message variance with the EKF2_EV*_NOISE values as a LOWER BOUND
#   EKF2_EV_DELAY  ms, reboot_required (applied before arming; the loader pushes at boot)
#
# No GNSS fusion at all (the sim sends no HIL_GPS in this mode anyway).
1	1	EKF2_GPS_CTRL	0	6
# Arming without a GPS lock is allowed (1 = warning only).
1	1	COM_ARM_WO_GPS	1	6
# sqrtVINS local-development profile: XYZ position, inertial velocity,
# and yaw (bits 0, 1, 2 and 3).
# Unlike frame-difference VO, sqrtVINS propagates velocity with the IMU.
# Keep the supplied 0.10 m/s velocity noise floor; no covariance tightening.
1	1	EKF2_EV_CTRL	15	6
# Height reference = external vision, matching the planner's map frame.
# Range-height aiding interpreted the 0.3048 m window sill as a new floor
# in run038, raising true height while PX4's z stayed fixed. Range remains
# published as a sensor, but EKF distance-to-ground validity is unavailable;
# landing speed is explicitly bounded below instead of relying on crawl mode.
1	1	EKF2_HGT_REF	3	6
1	1	EKF2_RNG_CTRL	0	6
# Indoors the magnetometer is unreliable; yaw comes from vision (EV_CTRL bit 3).
1	1	EKF2_MAG_TYPE	5	6
# TIME (review 2026-10-14, gps_denied/px4_clock.py): the bridge sends the CAPTURE
# time of each vision sample (stamp_mode:=capture), so the latency is in the
# stamp and EKF2_EV_DELAY describes only what the stamp misses (~0). It was
# 50 ms while the bridge sent RECEIPT time, which PX4's DDS client then
# clamped to 'now' anyway (its clock offset lagged the sim clock by 0-3.3 s).
1	1	EKF2_EV_DELAY	0.0	9
# Fusion horizon: EKF2_DELAY_MAX stays at PX4's DEFAULT 200 ms — it sizes the
# buffers at boot and this toolkit pushes the file AFTER boot, so a value
# here would not take effect. EKF2 fuses a sample at its own time while it
# is < 200 ms old, up to 100 ms late while it is < 300 ms old, never after
# (RingBuffer::pop_first_older_than); the bridge refuses captures > 0.3 s.
# Measured cuVSLAM capture age on PX4's clock, parked, RTF 0.77: p50 65-73 ms,
# p95 97-286 ms, max 372 ms (the tail is start-up).
# Use the variances the bridge puts in the message, bounded below by these.
1	1	EKF2_EV_NOISE_MD	0	6
1	1	EKF2_EVP_NOISE	0.05	9
1	1	EKF2_EVV_NOISE	0.10	9
1	1	EKF2_EVA_NOISE	0.05	9
# Quality gate: the bridge reports 0 when the source does not grade itself.
1	1	EKF2_EV_QMIN	0	6
# Indoor VIO flight envelope: slow. A VIO's error grows with optical flow rate
# and with how far the controller runs ahead of the estimate between frames.
1	1	MPC_XY_VEL_MAX	1.5	9
1	1	MPC_XY_CRUISE	1.0	9
1	1	MPC_ACC_HOR	1.0	9
1	1	MPC_Z_VEL_MAX_UP	1.0	9
1	1	MPC_Z_VEL_MAX_DN	0.7	9
# DEAD-RECKONING TIMEOUT (2026-10-16): after this long with no horizontal aiding (vision /
# flow) EKF2 reports the horizontal solution INVALID, and PX4's failsafe / AUTO_LAND fall
# back to a level vertical descent (Descend) instead of flying position control on IMU
# dead reckoning. The default (5 s) let a lost-vision landing run away at 4 m/s into a
# wall in 2 s (guard_maze_r1). Indoors there is nothing to recover to within 5 s; 1 s still
# rides through ordinary EV gaps (frames every 67 ms). Recommended for the real aircraft.
1	1	EKF2_NOAID_TOUT	1000000	6

# Local SITL cascade correction: inner XY velocity P=0.8 and attitude P=1.65
# come from the supplied airframe. The default outer position P=0.95 gives
# a weakly damped coupled loop. 0.35 proved too weak during liftoff;
# 0.65 retains more takeoff disturbance rejection while improving damping. See
# artifacts/diagnostics/position-loop-model.json; hardware is not qualified.
1	1	MPC_XY_P	0.65	9
# Range-height fusion is disabled, so PX4 dist_bottom_valid is false and native
# AUTO_LAND cannot select its range-triggered crawl speed. Run050 touched down
# at ~0.64 m/s and inverted. Bound descent independently of range availability.
# At 0.2 m/s, translational impact energy is ~8% of the 0.7 m/s default.
1	1	MPC_LAND_SPEED	0.2	9
1	1	MPC_LAND_CRWL	0.1	9
